LANGUAGE English

BOOK ClosePortal ORDERED NO KEEP LOOPED
    IF goal != goalClosePortal THEN EXIT

    // this hides the page since we are NO KEEP
    // this is easier than managing visibility
    MARK Step2Repeat READ

    PAGE Step1
        PROLOG "
            The portal is open and you must close it quickly. If you have the
            {c:QItemRitualKnife}, the {c:QItemRitualComponents}, and the
            {c:QItemElderSignPendant}, you can start now.
        
            Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can perform this ritual and only
            while standing at the altar.
        
            Are you ready?
        "

        BUTTON "Begin Ritual"

        TEXT "
            You flip to the correct place in the book, turn to face the altar,
			and lay out the materials. The pattern is complex and it takes a
			few minutes to get right. Your companions are under constant attack
			by cult members and you can feel the approach of something from the
			other side of the portal. You must hurry.
    
            Drop the {c:QItemRitualComponents} Unique Item on the altar. It
			must stay on the altar for the duration of the ritual.
    
            This step is complete.
        "
    END PAGE Step1

    PAGE Step2
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and again review the process for <<blessing>> the
			knife. When you glance down, you are suprised that you can read the
            words now.

            You pull out the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and...
        "

        BUTTON "Prepare the knife"

        TEXT "
            The book shows you how to hold the knife and some kind movement,
			like you>re presenting it to the altar. You fumble around, hoping
			your first try at something like this will be good enough.

            While you can read the words, you aren>t sure you understand them.
            If you do, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope for the
			best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "
		
		// even if we pass, we fail
        TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step2Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step2Fail
    END PAGE Step2

    PAGE Step2Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            As you finish the incantation, the blade becomes heavier and
			brighter. It... changes. The {c:QItemRitualKnife} is ready for
			what comes next.
        
            This step is complete
        "
    END PAGE Step2Pass

    PAGE Step2Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish the incantation but nothing seems to have happened.
			You>ll need to keep trying.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step2Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE Step2Fail

    PAGE Step2Repeat
        PROLOG "
            The knife still feels cold and dead in your hand. You're starting
			to wonder if you>>ll really be able to do this. You look at your
			fellow investigators, struggling to keep you alive and look down
			to try again.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            You read the text one more time, hold the knife over the altar,
            close your eyes, take a deep breath, and speak the words.

            If are certain you understand it now, test {lore}; otherwise, test
			{will} and hope for the best.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step2Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step2RepeatFail
    END PAGE Step2Repeat
	
    PAGE Step2RepeatFail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish again and... nothing. You take a breath to calm your
            nerves, but the noise and carnage across the room make it hard
			to focus.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step2Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE Step2RepeatFail

    PAGE Step3
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and see the next step: drawing blood. You have to
			cut yourself with the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and let the blood drip
			into the chalice on the altar. The book says that the blood will
			empower the ritual and to close the portal.
    
            You look at your hand and realize you are going to have to do this
			more than once. You steel yourself and prepare to draw blood.
        "

		BUTTON "Slice your palm"

        TEXT "
            You grip the {c:QItemRitualDagger} tightly and prepare to draw
			blood. You can feel your heart pounding in your chest. You must do
			this. You must stop the ritual.

            Test {will}. For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra
			die.
        "

        // even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step3Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step3Fail
    END PAGE Step3

    PAGE Step3Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You squeeze your hand into a tight fist and blood drips into the
			chalice. You can>t see or hear the chalice change, but you can feel
			something happen to it.

            This step is complete.
        "
    END PAGE Step3Pass

    PAGE Step3Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            A drop of blood spatters when it hits the cup. And another. Nothing
			seems to happen. You're going to have to slice deeper.
        
            Suffer 2 Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step3 UNREAD
    END PAGE Step3Fail

    PAGE Step4
        PROLOG "
            The portal is humming and pulsing with energy. You can feel
			something trying to get through from the other side. You must
			hurry. You turn the page and see the next incantation. Like the one
			for the dagger, blessing, you can read it, but you aren>t sure you
			understand it.
        "

        BUTTON "Read the incantation"

        TEXT "
            The incantation is long and complex. You>ll have to get this right
			to weaken the portal. If you don>t, it will take longer to close
			and the onslaught from the other side isn>t abating. You close your
			eyes for a moment, take a deep breath, look at the text again, and
			begin to speak the incantation.

            If you understand it, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope
			for the best.
       "
   
       // even if we pass, we fail
	   TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step4Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step4Fail
    END PAGE Step4

    PAGE Step4Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You feel a welling of power as you speak the last word. The feeling
            inside you grows and you suddenly feel like you control the cosmos.
            The portal grows brighter and {c:TokenPortal} screams. You had
            forgotten about the boy--he will die in this ritual.
        
            Suffer 1 facedown Horror.
        
            As the scream echos in the room, the portal grows dimmer and shrinks
            slightly. Where it was humming and stable before, it is sputtering,
            pulsing erratically, and making an electrical sound. It has been
            weakened, but not closed. It will eventually collapse on its own,
            but you can still feel something approaching. You can do better.
        
            This step is complete.
        "
    END PAGE Step4Pass

    PAGE Step4Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You can feel something happen inside but it is not very strong. The
			portal sputters for a moment, but nothing more. You>ll have to try
			the incantation again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Damage and 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).

            The ritual is wearing you down.
        "

        MARK Step4Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE Step4Fail

    PAGE Step4Repeat
        PROLOG "
            The portal is still humming and pulsing with energy. Whatever is
            approaching is getting closer.
        
            You look at the incantation again and take a deep, calming breath.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            Your fellow investigators are struggling to keep you alive and one
            looks over at you and you meet their eyes. Terror. Horror.  You
			must get this. You look back down at the text.
        
            If you understand it, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and hope
			for the best.
        "
        
		// even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step4Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step4Fail
    END PAGE Step4Repeat

    PAGE Step5
        PROLOG "
            You turn the page and see the next step: you>ll need more blood. You
            have to cut yourself again with the {c:QItemRitualDagger} and let the
            blood drip on to the {c:QItemElderSign}. The book says that the blood
            will empower the {c:QItemElderSign} to completely close the portal,
			and seal this ley line in a way that will prevent another portal
			from opening here ever again.
    
            You look at your hand and see that it has stopped bleeding. Cutting
            yourself again will take courage.
        "

        BUTTON "Draw more blood"

        TEXT "
            You draw your knife across your palm again and a searing pain
            momentarily overwhelms you. You have to do this.

            You look back down at the book and speak.

            If you understand the text, test {lore}; otherwise, test {will} and
            hope for the best.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        // even if we pass, we fail
		TEST QUOTA 10
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Fail
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE Step5

    PAGE Step5Pass
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You squeeze your hand into a tight fist over the trinket. As your
			blood drips, the it begins to glow. Then it and the knife begin
			pulsing. When you look up, you see the portal is dimmer and
			smaller, pulsing in sync with the {QItemRitualDagger} and the
			{c:QItemElderSign}. The boy screams again, no longer sounding
			human.

            The {c:QItemElderSign} rises and hovers over the altar. It vibrates
            briefly, then slowly moves across the room toward the portal.

            The boy screams one last time as the elder sign makes contact with
			his forehead. The boy goes rigid, then the portal collapses and the
			boy falls to the ground... still smoldering... still moaning.
        
            This investigation is over.
        "
		
        result = fullWin
        GOTO EventGameOverStart
    END PAGE Step5Pass

    PAGE Step5Fail
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        TEXT "
            You finish the incantation, but the {c:QItemElderSign} just lies
			there. You>ll have to try again.

            Suffer 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
        "

        MARK Step5Repeat UNREAD
    END PAGE Step5Fail

    PAGE Step5Repeat
        PAGE IS NOT VISIBLE

        PROLOG "
            You lift your hand over the altar again and prepare to speak again.
            The boy is still screaming in pain and terror.
        "

        BUTTON "Try again"

        TEXT "
            You squeeze more blood out of your fist on to the {c:QItemElderSign}.
            As it hits the trinket, the boy stops screaming.

            Test {lore} or {will}.
        
            For each Unique Item you have, you may roll 1 extra die.
        "

        TEST QUOTA 4
            ON PASS GOTO Step5Pass
            ON FAIL GOTO Step5Fail
    END PAGE Step5Repeat

END ClosePortal